     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my lucky bamboo leaves turning yellow?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yellow lucky bamboo leaves usually come from too much light or from the water. Direct sun scorches the leaves; chlorine and fluoride in tap water cause yellow and brown leaves and leaf drop; in soil, too much water turns the leaves yellow. Lower leaves also age and die naturally."
