      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A lucky bamboo stalk that turns soft has a disease or rot, and that part does not recover. A firm stalk that changes colour can simply be getting woody as it matures. Ohio State University Extension advises rooting a healthy top on its own, so a disease does not spread to the other stalks."
